VERDICTS
==================================================================================================
  V1 THE PER-CLUSTER y-TABLES: 12/12 clusters scored with the ZERO-PARAMETER dust law (c0 = -0.1445 anchored by the A_b = 0.650 infall jump, q = -1/3 derived from the G200 reservoir at 0.52 sigma, p = 0.99): log10 a_c = c0 + q log10(M500/8e14), amplitudes derived from M500 alone -- zero free parameters. The joint curves sit at median 2-bin slope -2.54 over [R500, 2R500] (-2.37 pointwise at 2 R500), the outer falloff steepened by the envelope's -0.99 relative to the phantom-only reading (-1.49).

  V2 THE EXPECTED-VERDICT TABLE: at the registered survey noise (Planck 143 all 12, ACT DR6 f150 the 7 in-band), the 3-way tree's per-cluster expectation is JOINT for 1/12, NEITHER for 2/12 (the steepest-gas pairs, A644-registered), PHANTOM-ONLY for 0/12 (a falsifier, never an expected outcome at the zero-param truth), INDECISIVE(grey) for 9/12 (the per-cluster error straddles branches -- the honest registered grey zone).  THE DECISION THE MEASUREMENT CARRIES IS SAMPLE-LEVEL (G177's registered design): the pooled 12-cluster 2-bin slope error 0.224 around the zero-param median -2.54 puts P(JOINT) = 0.75 (multi-bin 0.86) -- the tSZ run is EXPECTED to return JOINT at the sample level, with the F1'/F2' asymmetry registered (F2' dust-kill 4.4-6.9 sigma pooled strong, F1' 2.6 sigma weak).

  V3 THE HONEST STATEMENT: the tSZ test's final curves are fully zero-parameter -- the amplitude is the derived law (c0 from the A_b = 0.650 jump, q = -1/3 from the reservoir, the 0.52-sigma residual and the A_b 1.34x factor registered as the honest sliver), the shape is the framework's r^-1, the electron pressure is G113's registered phantom zone.  The expected verdicts are PRE-COMPUTED (JOINT 1/12 per-cluster; pooled P(JOINT) = 0.75, the decision point) and the first-run shortlist is NAMED: A3266, A2029, A85, A2319.  Uncertainty is fully owned: the y-tables are the prediction at zero free parameters, but the measurement's own verdict power is asymmetric (F2' strong, F1' weak -- the grey zone registered) -- the tSZ test can confidently pick JOINT, and can only point (not kill) toward NEITHER, exactly the G177 registered asymmetry carried into the final curves.
